// GRIP POINT ADJUSTMENT, FROM THE CONTROLLERS.
//
// A menu cannot do this: opening one pauses the game, so the gun you are adjusting stops
// being held the moment you go to adjust it, and the oval you are dragging is attached to
// a hand that is no longer moving. That is not a thing to work around in the menu; it is
// the reason not to use one.
//
// TWO KEYS. Hold the first and the sticks stop moving you and move the selected oval
// instead; let go and they are yours again, instantly. Tap the second to step to the next
// oval. Bind them to a shoulder and a face button.
//
// THE PLUS BELONGS IN THE BIND, NOT ONLY IN THE ALIAS. The engine sends a key-up event
// only for a binding whose command starts with '+', and it runs that command verbatim on
// the way down. Bound as the bare name it would look for an alias of exactly that name,
// find neither the + nor the - one, and do nothing at all -- bound, aliased, and silent.
// That cost a whole session on the body rig's adjust key (2026-09-25).
addmenusection "RS World Hands" 1
addmenukey "Grip points: adjust with the sticks (hold)" +rs_ovaledit
addmenukey "Grip points: next point"                    rs_ovalnext

alias +rs_ovaledit "netevent rs_ovaledit"
alias -rs_ovaledit "netevent rs_ovaledit_off"
alias rs_ovalnext  "netevent rs_ovalnext"
